# Final bounded Rabin lifecycle review

Accepted for the finite reviewed slice: actual root stage `work/backup-rabin-fixed-next`, `apps/backup/restic.mjs` SHA-256 `3b9473bea974df457a4ef40b33aa0ed0b4bade035bb300636005f323e02da176`, `capture-file.mjs` SHA-256 `c827d4c160cb3d57ba09717396d9ac44eebabf4aeaaaa64296a3ce65d94bbfa6`, and README SHA-256 `d56e2d3e29d6cb563940f49c1029f13e16f0b1f485f70133b3b450a229feae9f`. All 34 bound source files matched before and after review. Author-verifier output/receipt files are excluded from live source binding because root ran that verifier separately.

The unchanged 20-case lifecycle test source passed again, zero failures/skips. It covers both earlier cancellation boundaries through resolver and actual post-await named-file-stat injection; post-open cancellation with handle closure; deadline immediately before snapshot link with no snapshot/temp; deadline after link with committed success and cleanup; write/sync failures; primary plus temp/close cleanup errors; committed cleanup-warning visibility; own-lock release success/failure/missing outcomes; initializer and lock-writer warnings; and exclusive-temp collision preservation.

The three formerly failing pre-commit deadline diagnostics now assert zero subsequent I/O. Expiry after awaited temp mkdir started no open/write/sync. Expiry after open started no write/sync. Expiry after write started no sync. Every created temp handle closed, temporary files were removed, and no lock was published. Raw outputs and structured observations are retained. `precommit-deadline-observations.json` SHA-256 is `e0d30c6a31e5a6108fb03b4c055e864ba53708bb4acd831d48a0f14bb6f5805b`.

Prior evidence stays historical and unchanged: 164 files under `work/backup-rabin-fixed-review`, including its exact 52-file baseline, 20-pass receipt `741879c49af974703e218858f678c629f25b3dc6b3d49bbee7b8f11b1bd40f63`, three positive gap reproductions and preserved receipt-wrapper encoding failure. The final review uses a new exact source copy; it does not relabel prior failures as passes.

This acceptance is limited to the source-bound finite lifecycle slice. Test-only fault injection ran in this review process on owned synthetic files and was restored after each case. The close-error case deliberately reports a callback error after the real handle closes; it is not a proof about an uncloseable kernel handle. A deadline cannot forcibly interrupt already pending filesystem or sink work. File capture is not an atomic filesystem snapshot; failed capture can leave immutable unindexed packs. Actual cleanup failures remain observable warnings, and a failed own-lock removal can leave the exact reported lock. Calculated live capture buffers are not a hard process RSS limit. Full feature parity, comprehensive security, crash durability, rolling Cut runtime equivalence and performance superiority are not established here.

Root's separate original-boundary/author verification is separate evidence. This final independent batch reran 20 lifecycle cases and three strict deadline diagnostics, not the original application oracle. Original finite oracle and source arithmetic evidence remain attributed to the preceding exact-source review and root's separately source-bound run. No original stage, prior review, production or shared files were edited by this review.
